# ECC Framework Overview

Spec: EccFramework
Purpose:
  Synthesized summary of the Everything-Claude-Code (ECC) framework.
  Extracted from raw HTML resource (prompt 171-.md), converted to SDD spec format.

Owns: references/sdd/ecc-framework-overview.sdd

Source:
  ECC repository: https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC (MIT License)
  Article: https://www.datacamp.com/tutorial/everything-claude-code
  Date: 2026-06-29

FrameworkComponents:
  Claude Code:
    description: Underlying model interface by Anthropic
    role: Reads files, writes diffs, runs shell commands, calls tools
    note: ECC does NOT replace Claude Code — wraps around it

  AgentHarness:
    description: Specialized sub-agents with tool allowlists and scoped system prompts
    count: 66 agents (67 including loop-operator)
    examples:
      - planner: writes implementation blueprints (D1/D0 arm)
      - architect: system design, data model decisions (D1 arm)
      - code-reviewer: audits diffs with confidence threshold (R1 arm)
      - security-reviewer: OWASP-style pass (R1 arm)
      - build-error-resolver: fixes build errors (C1 arm)
      - e2e-runner: Playwright end-to-end tests (R1/DEP1 arm)
      - doc-updater: maintains codemaps (D1 arm)
      - loop-operator: orchestration coordination (supervisor role)

  SkillEcosystem:
    description: Reusable workflow instructions stored as Markdown SKILL.md files
    count: ~260 skills (ECC article) / 281 skills (ecc-bridge.sdd)
    location: skills/ directory at repo root, copied to ~/.claude/skills/
    examples:
      - tdd-workflow: red-green-refactor cycle
      - security-review: OWASP Top 10 audit, credential detection
      - frontend-patterns: React/Next.js conventions
      - django-patterns, django-tdd, django-security, django-verification
      - architect: system design reviews
      - golang-patterns, typescript-patterns, python-patterns

  WorkflowFramework:
    description: Hooks for tool events, rules that always apply, MCP configs, session memory
    hooks: 21 hook types (SessionStart, SessionStop, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, etc.)
    rules: 121 always-apply rules

  CommandsLayer:
    description: Maintained slash commands for common workflows
    command_count: 94 commands (per ecc-bridge.sdd)
    note: Backward-compatible shim folder for older command names

ContextAndMemory:
  SessionSummaries:
    trigger: Stop event hook
    storage: ~/.claude/sessions/
    content: what was worked on, what got decided, what's still open
    retention: configurable via ECC_SESSION_RETENTION_DAYS

  Instincts:
    description: Extracted patterns stored as instincts with confidence scores
    system: Continuous Learning v2
    commands: /instinct-status, /evolve

  LogFiles:
    location: ~/.claude/metrics/, ~/.claude/session-data/
    content: hook executions, skill runs, MCP calls, costs, errors

MCPSupport:
  protocol: Model Context Protocol (Anthropic standard)
  config_file: mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json
  default_enabled: chrome-devtools (1 server only)
  opt_in_required: GitHub, Supabase, Vercel, Railway, Linear, and others
  policy_date: June 2026 (reduced default-enabled servers to 1)

AgentShield:
  description: Standalone security auditor (npm package: ecc-agentshield)
  command: npx ecc-agentshield scan
  scan_categories: 5
    - Secrets detection: 14 patterns for hardcoded credentials
    - Permission auditing: tool/path grants, over-broad permissions
    - Hook injection analysis: exploit risk from hooks
    - MCP server risk profiling: read/write/call exposure
    - Agent config review: prompt injection, tool allowlist over-grants
  static_rules: 102
  internal_tests: 1,282
  coverage: 98%
  grades: A through F (letter grade)
  critical_exit_code: 2
  output_formats: terminal (color), JSON (CI), Markdown, HTML
  flags:
    -fix: auto-fix safe issues (remove secrets, tighten permissions)
    -opus: red-team/blue-team/auditor pipeline with Claude Opus 4.x
    -stream: live streaming analysis

Installation:
  method_plugin: Recommended for most users
    steps:
      - /plugin marketplace add https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC
      - /plugin install ecc@ecc
  method_manual:
    prerequisite: Claude Code v2.1.0+
    steps:
      - git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC.git
      - cp rules/common + language rules to ~/.claude/rules/ecc/
  caveat: Do NOT stack plugin + manual install (duplicate files)

Rules:
  [ECC-01] ECC agents have scoped tool allowlists — code-reviewer only reads files.
  [ECC-02] Context isolation: each sub-agent gets a clean context window.
  [ECC-03] MCP servers are opt-in by default (June 2026 policy).
  [ECC-04] AgentShield scans run as separate npm package, invokable via /security-scan.
  [ECC-05] Skills use confidence thresholds, not just binary pass/fail.

Navigation:
  References: @INDEX.sdd
  EccBridge: @../../agent/ecc-bridge.sdd

State: +
